infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title OTLP transport: gRPC vs HTTP/JSON
  desc Same protobuf schema, two transports — gRPC is the production default, HTTP/JSON the fallback
  compares
    - label OTLP/gRPC
      children
        - label Binary protobuf over HTTP/2
          desc The preferred service-to-Collector transport
        - label 50-70% smaller than JSON
          desc Fewer bytes on the wire per export batch
        - label 2-5x faster to encode
          desc Lower CPU cost per telemetry flush
        - label Supports streaming
          desc Multiplexed exports over one HTTP/2 connection
        - label Preferred edge contract
          desc Emit it and backends become Collector config
    - label OTLP/HTTP (JSON)
      children
        - label Protobuf or JSON over HTTP/1.1
          desc Same OTLP messages, simpler transport
        - label Largest, slowest variant
          desc JSON pays full text overhead vs binary
        - label No streaming
          desc One request per export batch
        - label Crosses gRPC-blocked firewalls
          desc Works where HTTP/2 / gRPC is dropped
        - label Browser-side telemetry
          desc The only option from the browser
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
